course: dictionary
lesson: 2848
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Dodge is a good example. «The goalkeeper had to dodge the ball» means moving quickly to one side so the ball does not hit you. The clue is that the goalkeeper is moving.
explain: Dodge can also mean avoiding something in a clever or sneaky way. «She tried to dodge my question about the broken vase» means she did not answer it. Nobody is running here, so the clue is what she is avoiding: the question.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If dodge means avoid, then «dodging chores» means avoiding chores, and that makes sense. Dodge can be a noun too: «It was a clever dodge» means a clever trick to avoid something.
fact: Dodge is a verb and a noun: you can dodge, or you can make a dodge.
fact: «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying, but it can hide things.»
fact: In a coyote chase, «the bird often dodges into a bush in time», which means it moves quickly to escape.
fact: Dodgeball is a game where players dodge the ball to avoid being hit.
fact: Other phrases with dodge: dodge the rain, dodge a question, dodge a job.
exercise: «The hero had to dodge the falling rock.» What does dodge mean here? | Sing a happy song | *Move quickly to one side to avoid being hit | Ask a question very loudly | Pick up and carry
exercise: «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying.» What does dodging a question mean? | Writing it down on paper | Answering it very loudly | *Avoiding it in a clever or sneaky way | Asking it again
exercise: What is a dodge? | A kind of ball used in games | A type of sock | *A quick move to one side, or a clever trick to avoid something | A loud shout
test: In the story, «she keeps it busy with a stick, dodging round a thistle» until the puppy tires. What is Alice doing? | Falling asleep under a tree | Feeding the puppy | *Moving quickly to avoid being caught | Singing a song to the thistle
test: Ella says, «I'll dodge the chores tonight.» What does she mean? | She will paint them bright colours | She will do them very fast | *She will try to avoid them | She will share them with her mum
exam: Which sentence uses dodge in the clever or sneaky sense? | «She dodged the rain under a tree.» | *«He tried to dodge my question about the cake.» | «I dodged the ball in the playground.» | «The fox dodged between the trees.»
